1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Build a 500mm x 900mm board to make a small quilt

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Rotate the quilt and let it be simulated on the ground

3
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Cut a layer to make the inflow effect, turn the surface over and let the front face all the way out

4
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Then select these two front and back panels

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Put pressure on the front and back panels

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Set pressure to 3 to make the inflow effect

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:10,000
If the inflow is slower, you can take off some panels manually to make the inflow more obvious

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Because we are making the quilt inside, the pressure 3 inflow is too obvious, so reduce it to 2

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Change the shape of the fabric line to Custom Angle

10
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
We need to make the curves more smooth on the sides

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Change the shape of the fabric line to Custom Angle

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Cut a layer to make the plate of the quilter be fit on the outside of the original plate

13
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Save some steps

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Then remove the joint of the newly created board and delete the sewing line

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Because the board has been turned over on the surface, so if the sewing line is not certain, you can separate the two boards and sew them with the sewing tool in the 3D window

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Then turn on the simulation

17
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:40,000
When the outer layer is smaller than the inner layer, the outer layer will be deformed, so it can be placed on the outer layer

18
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:48,000
When the outer layer is smaller than the inner layer, the outer layer can be placed on the outer layer

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
When there is two layers of boards, if the deformation is greater, it may be due to the wire gap cannot be penetrated

20
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
So it is necessary to get back to the starting point, the outer layer is only a little narrower

21
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:18,000
The center point of the double machine frame can activate center point function, and the following adjustments are based on the center point

22
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
I will explain it in more detail later

23
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:30,000
The outer layer of the back cover has been molded before, so it has the pressure of the original version, so you need to adjust the pressure of the outer layer to 0, because the back cover is usually single-layer and has no inflow.

24
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,000
If the back cover is pressed because of the pressure of the outer version, you can increase the pressure to 3.

25
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Add a new fabric and drag it to the selected panel, and apply the new fabric to the small quilt panel.

26
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Change the fabric to silk taffeta, which is a kind of synthetic fabric, which is easy to come out.

27
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Reduce the density of this fabric to make the weight of the panel lighter and easier to create the fluffy feeling of the quilt.

28
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Copy the inner fabric and increase the friction coefficient, so that when you make some random creases in the subsequent manual drag fabric, the creases will not dissipate due to the sliding of the fabric.

29
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Close the mat to make the desktop look more magnificent.

30
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Now we can place the curtain under the cover, and attach the most important part of the pápi.

31
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Lay the curtain on the back of the quilt at an angle at 1.5 inches, and push the pattern to the front from both sides.

32
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
You will get this pattern shown earlier.

33
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Place the curtain on the top of the pillow and press this moment to the top.

34
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
You can place the curtain over the block of the quilt and press it to the back of the pillow.

35
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
By doing this, the pattern of curtain will be better.

36
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
After you've placed the curtain on the back of the quilt, you can place the curtain on the top of the quilt, so that it will be easier to choose the draught.

37
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Contrary to the way of making the curtain, you can place the curtain on the back of the pillow.

38
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Turn the cup by hand to let the cup be in the right position

39
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:29,000
If the simulation speed is slow, you can press the simulation button to change to GPU simulation to deal with this part

40
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Reduce the example time to 8 to make it more detailed

41
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:58,000
After adjusting to the right position, press the W key to click on the tabletop

42
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
You can click on the tabletop again

43
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Add a fixed needle to the position of the tabletop to fix the small cup

44
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:21,000
After removing, pause the simulation and add a needle to maintain the effect of the fold before the fold disappears

45
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
The basic adjustment is that the friction coefficient of the surface is relatively high

46
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
If the friction coefficient is not high, the fold will soon disappear

47
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
And the fold will be more stable

48
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
In addition, it is easy to slip under GPU simulation

49
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:39,000
The fold will disappear when the friction coefficient is 30

50
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Press the W key to click on the fixed needle again to delete the fixed needle

51
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Thanks for watching

52
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
to get rid of more creases.

53
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Add some fixed creases to the position needle.

54
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
After the simulation is stable,

55
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
return to the default simulation tool

56
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
and simulate again.

57
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
After that, we can select these panels,

58
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
and delete the fixed creases on the panels

59
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
in the menu on the right.

60
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:32,000
When the simulation has stopped,

61
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
we can continue with the simulation.

